; word-gender-derivation-fourway.fk — a second, third and fourth pair of eyes on the
; part of the moon-gender derivation that can cross.
;
; The walkers read a self-contained source and have no `import`, so this cell composes
; the recipe the way the walkers need it — reads the derivation, appends the call,
; writes it once — and then host-execs the three siblings on it. No bash.
;
; What crosses: the mechanism the answer turns on. The composition computes the gender
; (axiom-3), the composition is read over the referent — Mädchen acks neuter over a girl
; — and three names of one referent disagree, so the referent bore none.
;
; What does not cross, named exactly: `nothing` is an unbound identifier in all three
; walkers (go, rust, ts alike), so every digit resting on axiom-1's third state stays
; native-only. That is a hole in the proof organ, not in this cell: no cell that honors
; nothing as first-class can currently reach a second pair of eyes. Named here as the
; next stone; see receipts/2026-07-28-the-moon-was-never-masculine.md.
;
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/four-way-run.fk form/form-stdlib/form-fs.fk
; witnessed: 2026-07-28 -> 0 (FOUR-WAY), all four kernels at 11111
import "../word-gender-derivation.fk"
(do
    (let recipe "/tmp/word-gender-shape-recipe.fk")
    (write_file recipe
        (str_concat (read_file "cognition/word-gender-derivation.fk")
                    "\n(word-gender-shape-check)\n"))
    (fr-diagnose
        (str_concat "./walkers/go/walker " recipe)
        (str_concat "./walkers/rust/target/release/form-walker-rust " recipe)
        (str_concat "node --experimental-strip-types walkers/ts/main.ts " recipe)
        (word-gender-shape-check)))
